inimum of five years of feeling  that they couldn't speak openly or they  couldn't speak freely so there's no  question at all that the tide is turning  and that something has changed in the  air I think that then the next steps  forward are that not only do we continue  to question but within the class within  the academic environment but we also do  so in a way that's civil and polite and  respectful we never want to lose that in  our society and we've seen the  consequences of that already so reason  has been slapped around and people feel  rightly so that they haven't been able  to speak out and in a way that  accords with their conscience and the  step to get back to those values I think  is to continue to attempt to be civil  and have an honest conversation with  somebody and if you're met with rage or  anger the response is not to meet  someone through age or anger  I'll keep doing it if you guys keep  doing it fair we'll keep doing it and  we're not quitting alright follow these  guys on Twitter it's at conceptual James  and at Peter Bogosian and we'll link to  where you want me to link to one of the  videos mike-mike Naina's youtube channel  is the place to go if you want to see  what we're up to what we've been up to  what we've done what he's putting out  it's all in the same theme he's his  YouTube channels our hub and great don't  miss it we're gonna have a link to that  right down below  [Music]
 

